      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html lang='en'><head><meta charset='UTF-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0'><title>Self-Loop Bottleneck</title><style>*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}body{font-family:'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;background:#0d1117;color:#e6edf3;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;padding:30px;min-height:100vh}h1{font-size:1.5rem;color:#58a6ff;margin-bottom:6px}p.sub{color:#8b949e;font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:30px;text-align:center;max-width:600px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,1fr);gap:16px;max-width:740px;width:100%}.card{background:#161b22;border-radius:12px;padding:16px;text-align:center;transition:transform .2s,box-shadow .2s;cursor:default}.card:hover{transform:translateY(-4px);box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,.5)}.card.perfect{border:2px solid #f97583}.card.imperfect{border:2px solid #79c0ff}.card h3{font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:4px}.card .semi{color:#8b949e;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:12px}.loops-container{position:relative;height:180px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;align-items:center}.bar{width:36px;border-radius:6px 6px 0 0;transition:height .8s cubic-bezier(.34,1.56,.64,1)}.bar.perfect-bar{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f97583,#b62324)}.bar.imperfect-bar{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#79c0ff,#1f6feb)}.count{font-size:2rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:8px}.type-label{font-size:.75rem;margin-top:4px;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:4px;display:inline-block}.type-label.p{background:#f9758330;color:#f97583}.type-label.i{background:#79c0ff30;color:#79c0ff}.ratio-box{margin-top:30px;background:#161b22;border-radius:12px;padding:20px 32px;text-align:center;max-width:500px}.ratio-box h2{color:#f0883e;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:8px}.ratio-box p{color:#8b949e;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6}</style></head><body><h1>The Self-Loop Bottleneck</h1><p class='sub'>Perfect consonances admit exactly <strong style='color:#f97583'>1</strong> self-loop (the identity). Imperfect consonances admit <strong style='color:#79c0ff'>12</strong>. This 12× disparity is why parallel fifths are forbidden.</p><div class='grid' id='grid'></div><div class='ratio-box'><h2>Bottleneck Ratio: 1 : 12</h2><p>A perfect consonance (unison or fifth) can only sustain itself by <em>not moving</em>. An imperfect consonance (third or sixth) has 12 different ways to persist — one for each possible bass motion. This forces composers to <em>pass through</em> perfect consonances rather than linger on them.</p></div><script>const data=[{name:'Unison',semi:0,type:'perfect',loops:1},{name:'m3',semi:3,type:'imperfect',loops:12},{name:'M3',semi:4,type:'imperfect',loops:12},{name:'P5',semi:7,type:'perfect',loops:1},{name:'m6',semi:8,type:'imperfect',loops:12},{name:'M6',semi:9,type:'imperfect',loops:12}];const grid=document.getElementById('grid');data.forEach((d,i)=>{const card=document.createElement('div');card.className=`card ${d.type}`;const maxH=150,h=d.loops/12*maxH;card.innerHTML=`<h3>${d.name}</h3><div class='semi'>${d.semi} semitones</div><div class='loops-container'><div class='bar ${d.type}-bar' style='height:0px;width:36px' id='bar${i}'></div></div><div class='count'>${d.loops}</div><span class='type-label ${d.type==='perfect'?'p':'i'}'>${d.type}</span>`;grid.appendChild(card);setTimeout(()=>{document.getElementById('bar'+i).style.height=Math.max(h,8)+'px'},100+i*120)})</script></body></html>"
