lass=\"explanation\">A <strong>self-loop</strong> is a voice leading where both voices move but the interval stays the same. For a <strong>perfect consonance</strong> (unison or fifth), only the identity — both voices holding still — is allowed. Any parallel motion (both voices moving identically) into a perfect consonance is <em>forbidden</em>. For an <strong>imperfect consonance</strong> (thirds and sixths), all 12 parallel motions are permitted. This 12:1 ratio is the quantitative signature of the parallel-fifths rule.</p></div><script>const data=[{name:'Unison',interval:0,perfect:true,loops:1},{name:'Minor 3rd',interval:3,perfect:false,loops:12},{name:'Major 3rd',interval:4,perfect:false,loops:12},{name:'Perfect 5th',interval:7,perfect:true,loops:1},{name:'Minor 6th',interval:8,perfect:false,loops:12},{name:'Major 6th',interval:9,perfect:false,loops:12}];const grid=document.getElementById('grid');data.forEach(d=>{const card=document.createElement('div');card.className='card';const bars=Array.from({length:12},(_,i)=>{const active=i<d.loops;const h=active?80:8;const color=active?(d.perfect?'#ff6b6b':'#51cf66'):'#222';return`<div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:${h}px;background:${color}\"></div>`}).join('');card.innerHTML=`<h3>${d.name} (${d.interval})</h3><div class=\"type\">${d.perfect?'PERFECT':'IMPERFECT'} consonance</div><div class=\"bar-container\">${bars}</div><div class=\"count\" style=\"color:${d.perfect?'#ff6b6b':'#51cf66'}\">${d.loops}</div><div style=\"font-size:.8em;color:#888\">self-loop${d.loops!==1?'s':''}</div>`;grid.appendChild(card)})</script></body></html>"
