      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0\"><title>Self-Loop Bottleneck</title><style>*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}body{background:#1a1a2e;color:#e0e0e0;font-family:'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;min-height:100vh;padding:20px}h1{font-size:1.4em;margin-bottom:5px;color:#e8d44d}h2{font-size:0.85em;font-weight:normal;color:#888;margin-bottom:20px;text-align:center;max-width:600px}.container{display:flex;gap:30px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:20px}.card{background:#16213e;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;width:260px;text-align:center;transition:transform 0.2s}.card:hover{transform:translateY(-3px)}.card h3{font-size:1em;margin-bottom:10px}.card .count{font-size:4em;font-weight:bold;margin:10px 0}.card.perfect .count{color:#e8d44d}.card.imperfect .count{color:#4fc3f7}.card .label{font-size:0.8em;color:#888;margin-bottom:15px}.bar-container{width:100%;margin-top:10px}.bar{height:24px;border-radius:4px;transition:width 1s ease;position:relative}.bar span{position:absolute;right:8px;top:3px;font-size:0.75em;font-weight:bold}.intervals{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;justify-content:center;margin-top:12px}.interval{background:#0f0f23;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:15px;font-size:0.8em}.ratio-box{background:#16213e;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;max-width:560px;width:100%;text-align:center;margin-top:10px}.ratio-box .big{font-size:2.5em;font-weight:bold;color:#ff7043;margin:10px 0}.explanation{max-width:560px;margin-top:15px;font-size:0.85em;line-height:1.6;color:#aaa;text-align:center}</style></head><body><h1>🎵 The Self-Loop Bottleneck</h1><h2>Why parallel fifths are forbidden: perfect consonances admit only 1 self-loop vs 12 for imperfect consonances</h2><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"card perfect\"><h3>Perfect Consonances</h3><div class=\"count\" id=\"pCount\">0</div><div class=\"label\">self-loop(s) each</div><div class=\"bar-container\"><div class=\"bar\" id=\"pBar\" style=\"width:0%;background:#e8d44d\"><span></span></div></div><div class=\"intervals\"><span class=\"interval\">P1 (0)</span><span class=\"interval\">P5 (7)</span></div></div><div class=\"card imperfect\"><h3>Imperfect Consonances</h3><div class=\"count\" id=\"iCount\">0</div><div class=\"label\">self-loops each</div><div class=\"bar-container\"><div class=\"bar\" id=\"iBar\" style=\"width:0%;background:#4fc3f7\"><span></span></div></div><div class=\"intervals\"><span class=\"interval\">m3 (3)</span><span class=\"interval\">M3 (4)</span><span class=\"interval\">m6 (8)</span><span class=\"interval\">M6 (9)</span></div></div></div><div class=\"ratio-box\"><div style=\"color:#888;font-size:0.9em\">Bottleneck Ratio</div><div class=\"big\">1 : 12</div><div style=\"color:#888;font-size:0.9em\">A perfect consonance is 12× more constrained</div></div><div class=\"explanation\"><p>A <b style=\"color:#e8d44d\">self-loop</b> is a voice leading that preserves the current interval. For a self-loop (b, s), we need s = b (both voices move the same amount). At a <b style=\"color:#e8d44d\">perfect</b> consonance, this is <em>parallel motion into a perfect consonance</em> — forbidden unless b = 0 (no motion). At an <b style=\"color:#4fc3f7\">imperfect</b> consonance, parallel motion is unrestricted, so all 12 values of b work.</p><p style=\"margin-top:10px\">This is the mathematical reason why parallel fifths and octaves are forbidden in classical counterpoint: they would require self-loops that don't exist in the quiver.</p></div><script>setTimeout(()=>{document.getElementById('pCount').textContent='1';document.getElementById('iCount').textContent='12';document.getElementById('pBar').style.width=(1/12*100)+'%';document.getElementById('iBar').style.width='100%'},300)</script></body></html>"
