type=\"number\" value=\"3\" min=\"1\" max=\"10\"></div><div class=\"cg\"><label>D</label><input id=\"catD\" type=\"number\" value=\"2\" min=\"2\" max=\"10\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" id=\"catResult\"></div><div class=\"theorem-box\"><strong>Theorem (catalog_impossibility):</strong> For D ≥ 2 and A<sup>L</sup> ≥ 1, we have |Vol(A,L)| &lt; |CatalogScheme(A,L,D)|.<br><strong>Theorem (no_catalog_embedding):</strong> No injection f : CatalogScheme → Vol exists.<br><strong>Theorem (babel_cantor):</strong> No surjection g : Vol → CatalogScheme exists.</div></div><div class=\"panel\"><h3>2. Compression Limits (incompressible_ge_compressible)</h3><div class=\"controls\"><div class=\"cg\"><label>A</label><input id=\"compA\" type=\"number\" value=\"3\" min=\"2\" max=\"6\"></div><div class=\"cg\"><label>L (original)</label><input id=\"compL\" type=\"number\" value=\"5\" min=\"2\" max=\"12\"></div><div class=\"cg\"><label>M (compressed)</label><input id=\"compM\" type=\"number\" value=\"3\" min=\"1\" max=\"11\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" id=\"compResult\"></div><div class=\"theorem-box\"><strong>Theorem (incompressible_ge_compressible):</strong> For A ≥ 2 and M &lt; L, any compression–decompression cycle loses at least as many volumes as it preserves: |{v | decompress(compress(v)) ≠ v}| ≥ |{v | decompress(compress(v)) = v}|.</div></div><div class=\"panel\"><h3>3. Periodic Structure (periodic_volume_count)</h3><div class=\"controls\"><div class=\"cg\"><label>A</label><input id=\"perA\" type=\"number\" value=\"3\" min=\"1\" max=\"6\"></div><div class=\"cg\"><label>L</label><input id=\"perL\" type=\"number\" value=\"12\" min=\"1\" max=\"20\"></div></div><div class=\"result\" id=\"perResult\"></div><div class=\"theorem-box\"><strong>Theorem (periodic_volume_count):</strong> For p | L, the number of p-periodic volumes is exactly A<sup>p</sup>.</div></div></div><script>function updateCatalog(){const A=Math.max(2,parseInt(document.getElementById('catA').value)||2);const 