class='ldot' style='background:#51cf66'></div>Imperfect consonance</div></div><div class='ratio-box'><h3>Ratio: 12 to 1</h3><p>A perfect consonance (unison, perfect fifth) admits <strong>exactly 1</strong> self-loop — the identity, where neither voice moves. An imperfect consonance (thirds, sixths) admits <strong>all 12</strong> self-loops: any parallel motion preserves the interval without penalty.<br><br>This is why parallel fifths are forbidden: the mathematics leaves no room for motion.</p></div><script>const data=[{name:'Unison',sub:'(P1/P8)',val:1,type:'perfect'},{name:'Minor 3rd',sub:'(m3)',val:12,type:'imperfect'},{name:'Major 3rd',sub:'(M3)',val:12,type:'imperfect'},{name:'Perfect 5th',sub:'(P5)',val:1,type:'perfect'},{name:'Minor 6th',sub:'(m6)',val:12,type:'imperfect'},{name:'Major 6th',sub:'(M6)',val:12,type:'imperfect'}];const chart=document.getElementById('chart');const maxVal=12;data.forEach((d,i)=>{const g=document.createElement('div');g.className='bar-group';const w=document.createElement('div');w.className='bar-wrap';const b=document.createElement('div');b.className=`bar ${d.type}`;b.style.height='0px';b.textContent=d.val;w.appendChild(b);const l=document.createElement('div');l.className='label';l.textContent=d.name;const sl=document.createElement('div');sl.className='sublabel';sl.textContent=d.sub;g.appendChild(w);g.appendChild(l);g.appendChild(sl);chart.appendChild(g);setTimeout(()=>{b.style.height=(d.val/maxVal*280)+'px'},100+i*150)})</script></body></html>"
